& [CanonicalRecord: LangSOPInitialWorkflow] is the processed initial planning authority for LangSOP
  + [canonical_uuid] is b4f65971-1324-4228-9193-8d395704ccf7
  + [source_uuid] is 72626309-1ab9-4e26-9d59-5ad35d8e9f36
  + [exploded_uuid] is ef0c7679-4c7d-4773-bd8d-e567018a7648
  + [authority_scope] is initial architecture, layer responsibilities, whole-field planning model, candidate compiled duties, candidate LangGraph shape, development stages, and model routing policy
  + [implementation_scope] is specification only; no runtime operator, storage schema, or LangGraph execution has been implemented by this canonical record
  + [satisfaction_signature] is [SatisfactionSignature: LangSOPInitialWorkflow]

  = must: treat this file as the current processed planning authority for LangSOP until superseded or invalidated
  = must: consult the exploded specification for derivation detail and open questions
  = must: preserve the dictated source document unchanged
  = must: invalidate this canonical record if the source hash changes without reprocessing

& [CanonicalLayerContract: LangSOPInitialWorkflow] is the stable layer split
  + [sop_layer] is semantic proof, source preservation, specification authority, SJS processing, reconsideration, invalidation, and soft-wire debugging
  + [authority_kernel_layer] is typed durable records for source logs, narrative anchors, capability fields, support, authority, proof, coordination, readiness, and work packets
  + [langgraph_layer] is executable procedure over authority kernel records
  + [surface_layer] is projections and adapters for human, agent, chat, dashboard, terminal, Codex, Langflow, and other interfaces
  + [judgment_layer] is human or model reasoning for ambiguous, high-risk, semantic, or authority-changing work

  = must: keep truth-bearing authority in SOP and authority kernel records
  = must: use LangGraph for procedural workflow execution, not as the sole truth model
  = must: use surface tools as projections and input channels, not as canonical authority
  = must: route semantic repair and authority changes back to SOP-first processing

& [CanonicalWholeFieldPlanningContract] is the initial replacement for premature slice-first planning
  + [planning_primitive] is capability_field
  + [execution_primitive] is work_packet
  + [capability_node] is the central planning record
  + [blocked_objective] is allowed as a first-class capability node before packetization
  + [readiness_projection] is a derived view, not source authority

  = must: articulate the whole capability field before creating worker-sized packets
  = must: generate work packets on demand from readiness, support, authority, proof, dependency, ownership, and risk conditions
  = must: update the capability field after completion review before generating the next packet
  - never: treat a generated work packet as replacing the capability field
  - never: mark blocked or unsupported objectives ready merely to keep workers busy

& [CanonicalCompiledDutyPolicy] is the first compilation policy for SOP duties
  + [compile_when] is stable, frequent, mechanically checkable, typed inputs and outputs are known, and a trace or proof oracle exists
  + [stay_sop_first_when] is meaning, ambiguity, authority, architecture, requirement mutation, proof interpretation, or narrative reframing is active
  + [operator_trace] is required evidence that a compiled duty behaved according to its SOP source

  = must: compile repetitive governance into kernel operators or LangGraph nodes only when contracts are stable
  = must: preserve compiled operator output as derived state with lineage to source and operator trace
  = must: return to SOP when compiled behavior conflicts with source meaning or encounters unknown state

& [CanonicalInitialDataSubjects] is the initial kernel data vocabulary
  + [source_log] is the append-only evidence stream of what happened
  + [log_entry] is one citable unit in source_log
  + [citation_ref] is a stable reference from a derived claim to source evidence
  + [narrative_node] is a durable unit of project meaning or story state
  + [understanding_anchor] is an agent's explicit working interpretation and support basis
  + [capability_node] is one desired, blocked, ready, implemented, or verified capability in the whole field
  + [requirement_record] is an atomic obligation belonging to a capability
  + [support_record] is evidence supporting a requirement
  + [authority_artifact] is a source document, canonical specification, proof, signature, solution, or registry record
  + [coordination_claim] is an agent, user, or process claim over work boundaries, proof, review, or frontier
  + [work_packet] is an on-demand executable packet generated from current readiness
  + [completion_review] is the record that evaluates completed work for support_delta, requirement_delta, stale state, proof, and next frontier
  + [readiness_projection] is a generated view of packetizable and blocked work

  = must: define natural keys before storage implementation
  = must: separate source data from derived projections
  = must: preserve freshness and invalidation rules for derived projections

& [CanonicalInitialLangGraphShape] is the first procedural target
  + [graph_name] is WholeFieldPlannerGraph
  + [node] is SourceIntakeNode
  + [node] is DelineationNode
  + [node] is CapabilityFieldNode
  + [node] is DataDesignNode
  + [node] is RequirementSupportNode
  + [node] is AuthorityClassificationNode
  + [node] is ReadinessProjectionNode
  + [node] is WorkPacketGeneratorNode
  + [node] is HumanReviewInterrupt
  + [node] is DispatchNode
  + [node] is CompletionReviewNode
  + [node] is NarrativeUpdateNode
  + [node] is SJSUpdateNode
  + [node] is RecomputeReadinessNode

  = must: treat nodes as operators over kernel records
  = must: keep graph checkpoints as resumable execution state rather than authority
  = must: expose interrupts for unresolved authority or ambiguity

& [CanonicalDevelopmentFrontier] is the ordered initial work frontier
  + [frontier_1] is define kernel data schemas for capability_node, requirement_record, support_record, authority_artifact, work_packet, completion_review, and readiness_projection
  + [frontier_2] is choose first storage backend and preservation rules for source logs and kernel records
  + [frontier_3] is define operator contracts for signature_validation, support_readiness_recompute, work_packet_generation, completion_delta_review, and stale_projection_detection
  + [frontier_4] is implement a minimal LangGraph proof-of-shape over fixture kernel records
  + [frontier_5] is add a surface layer that renders manager view, worker packet, blocker view, and narrative/debug view from kernel records
  + [frontier_6] is compile one existing ReasoningFramework duty end-to-end and compare operator trace against SOP source expectations
  + [frontier_7] is design operations-manager integration for the target Ryzen 9 RTX 5090 machine after authority and packetization semantics stabilize

  = must: complete frontier_1 through frontier_3 before relying on LangGraph as workflow authority
  = should: treat frontier_1 through frontier_3 as requiring deeper reasoning
  = should: split frontier_4 and later bounded implementation work into Spark-suitable packets after contracts stabilize

& [Justification: LangSOPInitialWorkflow] is the evidence bridge for accepting this initial canonical specification
  + [claim] is LangSOP is ready for initial staged specification and schema design
  + [support] is preserved source document, source hash, exploded specification, stable layer split, whole-field planning contract, compiled-duty policy, data subject vocabulary, LangGraph target shape, and explicit development frontier
  + [confidence] is high for the architecture split between SOP, kernel, LangGraph, surfaces, and model judgment
  + [confidence] is moderate for exact storage backend, first operator set, Langflow role, and runtime implementation order because those remain open design decisions
  + [counterargument] is LangGraph may absorb more authority-shaped state than expected if the kernel contract is underspecified
  + [invalidation_condition] is source_change, failed_schema_design, operator_contract_conflict, hidden_authority_state, LangGraph_checkpoint_treated_as_authority, or implementation_contradiction

  ! [LangSOPInitialWorkflowAcceptedForPlanning] is accepted
    @ [support] [CanonicalLayerContract: LangSOPInitialWorkflow]
    @ [support] [CanonicalWholeFieldPlanningContract]
    @ [support] [CanonicalDevelopmentFrontier]
    @ [support] [SatisfactionSignature: LangSOPInitialWorkflow]

